# The ledger of `tokenizer`: what Go's
# tiktoken-go (github.com/pkoukk/tiktoken-go v0.1.8), Rust's tiktoken-rs
# (0.12.1) and Python's tiktoken (0.14.0, OpenAI's own) and Hugging Face's
# tokenizers (0.23.3, the Python face of the Rust crate of that name) let a
# program do with the tokens of a model, one block per capability, and what
# Rebel answers. No standard library of the three tokenizes. The encodings
# carried as data, and which a model reads, are `tokenizer/tables`'s, in its
# own ledger, `tokenizer/tables.ledger`, since 2026-11-19.
#
# The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-18: `go doc -all` of tiktoken-go
# fetched into the scratch folder; the items of `cargo doc` of tiktoken-rs,
# its functions, structs, constants and `CoreBPE`'s methods; and `dir()` of
# `tiktoken`, `tiktoken.Encoding`, `tiktoken.load`, `tiktoken.model`,
# `tiktoken.registry`, `tiktoken_ext.openai_public`, `tokenizers`,
# `tokenizers.Tokenizer`, `tokenizers.Encoding` and the six modules of
# `tokenizers`, each installed into the scratch folder.
#
# The tests hold tiktoken's tokens, in `o200k_base` and `cl100k_base`, for
# 204 texts of sixteen scripts, emoji, marks, digits of four scripts, every
# kind of white space, code and runs of one character, each decoded back;
# and tiktoken's answers for an encoding of 268 tokens made by `new` and by
# `tiktoken.Encoding` alike. The differential outside the tests, 2026-11-18:
# 23,006 generated texts, 2.76 MB (mixtures of those fragments and random
# assigned code points of nine ranges of the planes, and runs of one
# character of 100 KB), every one made the same tokens as tiktoken 0.14.0 in
# both encodings and decoded back. Speed, the same day on this Mac, a
# megabyte of many scripts in `o200k_base` built at -O2: 0.30 s with the
# table read (0.05 s), against tiktoken's 0.055 s; two megabytes of one
# letter, one piece, 1.3 s and 116 MB, against tiktoken's 0.33 s.

capability tok/new  an encoding made from its tokens, its pattern and its special tokens
  heroes  tokenizer.new, tokenizer.Encoding
  go      NewCoreBPE, CoreBPE, NewTiktoken, Tiktoken, Encoding
  rust    CoreBPE::new, CoreBPE, Rank, FromRank
  python  tiktoken.Encoding, tokenizers.Tokenizer, tokenizers.models.BPE, tokenizers.models.Model
  note    every byte must be a token, alone, so that any text can be encoded: a table without one is refused when it is made, where tiktoken 0.14.0 makes it and panics when a text needs the byte (observed 2026-11-18: `PanicException: no entry found for key`). Two special texts may share a number, as tiktoken lets them and its `o200k_harmony` does (200018): both encode to it and it decodes to the text given first, which is the one tiktoken decodes. tokenizers' BPE merges by a list of pairs ranked, where tiktoken merges by the rank of the bytes the pair makes; the two agree on vocabularies made byte by byte, and this package reads the second

capability tok/ranks-file  the `.tiktoken` file of a vocabulary read and written
  heroes  tokenizer.parse_ranks, tokenizer.format_ranks
  go      BpeLoader, NewDefaultBpeLoader, SetBpeLoader
  rust    -
  python  tiktoken.load.load_tiktoken_bpe, tiktoken.load.dump_tiktoken_bpe, tiktoken.load.read_file
  note    a file is read with `read_file` or `fs`; fetched from a URL with `http`; its SHA-256 checked with `crypto`. tiktoken's reader keeps one line a token in any order; here too, and a rank given twice or a gap below the largest is `invalid`, the line named

capability tok/ranks-fetched  a vocabulary fetched by URL, cached on disk, its hash checked
  heroes  refused: three packages compose to it, `http` fetches, `fs` keeps, `crypto` hashes; the tables of OpenAI's encodings are carried as data and need no fetch
  go      NewDefaultBpeLoader
  rust    -
  python  tiktoken.load.read_file_cached, tiktoken.load.check_hash
  note    -

capability tok/gpt2-files  GPT-2's `vocab.bpe` and `encoder.json` read into a vocabulary
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tiktoken.load.data_gym_to_mergeable_bpe_ranks
  note    the ranks those two files make are `r50k_base`'s; reading `encoder.json` needs `json`, a package of this package's own layer (README § A1), so it waits for the older tables (`tokenizer/tables.ledger`'s tok/older-tables)

capability tok/encode  a text made tokens, special tokens' texts refused
  heroes  tokenizer.encode
  go      Tiktoken.Encode
  rust    CoreBPE::encode, CoreBPE::encode_as, EncodeError
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode, tokenizers.Tokenizer.encode, tokenizers.Encoding.ids, tokenizers.Encoding.tokens
  note    tiktoken's default: a text that holds `<|endoftext|>` from outside must not end a prompt early. Refused `invalid`, the special token and its byte index named, where tiktoken raises ValueError

capability tok/encode-ordinary  a text made tokens, special tokens' texts read as text
  heroes  tokenizer.encode_ordinary
  go      Tiktoken.EncodeOrdinary
  rust    CoreBPE::encode_ordinary, CoreBPE::encode_ordinary_as
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode_ordinary
  note    the pattern is matched by hand for tiktoken's two patterns and by `regex` for any other (tok/pre-tokenize); the tests hold the two ways to the same pieces

capability tok/encode-specials  special tokens allowed and refused by the caller
  heroes  tokenizer.encode_with_specials
  go      Tiktoken.Encode, Tiktoken.SpecialTokenRegex
  rust    CoreBPE::encode_with_special_tokens, CoreBPE::encode_with_special_tokens_as, CoreBPE::special_tokens
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode, tokenizers.Tokenizer.encode_special_tokens, tokenizers.AddedToken
  note    tiktoken's `allowed_special` and `disallowed_special`, "all" written `special_tokens(enc)`; a special token neither allowed nor refused is read as text, as in tiktoken. A name that is no special token of the encoding fails `invalid`, so a misspelt one is told; where two allowed special tokens begin at one place the longer is taken

capability tok/count  the tokens of a text counted
  heroes  tokenizer.count
  go      -
  rust    CoreBPE::count, CoreBPE::count_ordinary, CoreBPE::count_with_special_tokens
  python  -
  note    `encode_ordinary`'s count; a count with special tokens allowed is the length of `encode_with_specials`'s answer. Python counts with `len` of `encode`

capability tok/claude  the tokens of a text counted as Claude reads them
  heroes  anthropic.count_tokens
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Anthropic publishes no tokenizer for Claude: its tokens are counted by the API's `count_tokens`, which `llm/anthropic` asks over the network; no table of this package counts them

capability tok/truncate  a text cut to at most a number of tokens
  heroes  tokenizer.truncate
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenizers.Tokenizer.enable_truncation, tokenizers.Tokenizer.no_truncation, tokenizers.Tokenizer.truncation, tokenizers.Encoding.truncate, tokenizers.Encoding.overflowing
  note    tokenizers cuts the list of ids; here the text is cut, never inside a character, and the cut moves back a token at a time until the text re-encodes within the count, since a cut piece may encode otherwise. Overlapping windows of a text are `chunks`'

capability tok/pre-tokenize  the pieces a pattern cuts a text into before merging
  heroes  tokenizer.pieces_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Split, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.ByteLevel, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.PreTokenizer, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Sequence, tokenizers.PreTokenizedString, tokenizers.Regex, tokenizers.SplitDelimiterBehavior
  note    the pattern is fancy-regex's dialect as tiktoken writes it, read by `regex` (`tokenizer/internal/dialect`): `\s` as Unicode's White_Space, possessives as greedy, the look-ahead `\s+(?!\S)` as a whole alternative in two steps; any other look-around, `\w`, `\b` and a class inside a class fail `unsupported`. `regex` reads a quarter of a megabyte a second on these patterns, so tiktoken's two are also matched by hand, about twenty times faster, and held to `regex`'s pieces by the tests. Character classes are Unicode 17.0.0's, `unicode`'s

capability tok/pre-tokenize-other  tokenizers' other pre-tokenizers: by white space, punctuation, digits, script, a fixed length, Metaspace, BERT's
  heroes  refused: each is a pattern `new` reads, or a cut of `strings` and `unicode/segment`; this package is tiktoken's byte-pair encoding (README § A1)
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Whitespace, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.WhitespaceSplit, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Punctuation, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Digits, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.UnicodeScripts, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.FixedLength, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.Metaspace, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.CharDelimiterSplit, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.BertPreTokenizer
  note    -

capability tok/single-token  the token that is exactly some bytes
  heroes  tokenizer.token_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode_single_token, tokenizers.Tokenizer.token_to_id
  note    an ordinary or special token; absent is `not_found`, where tiktoken raises KeyError

capability tok/piece  bytes merged as one piece, with no pattern
  heroes  tokenizer.encode_piece
  go      -
  rust    byte_pair_split
  python  tiktoken.Encoding._encode_single_piece
  note    bytes that are not UTF-8 too; no bytes answer no token, where tiktoken 0.14.0 panics (observed: "range end index 2 out of range"). tiktoken-rs answers the bytes of each part, `decode_tokens` of this answer

capability tok/decode  tokens made text
  heroes  tokenizer.decode
  go      Tiktoken.Decode
  rust    CoreBPE::decode, DecodeKeyError
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.decode, tokenizers.Tokenizer.decode, tokenizers.decoders.ByteLevel, tokenizers.decoders.Decoder
  note    bytes that are not UTF-8 replaced by U+FFFD by Python's rule, tiktoken's default (`errors="replace"`), through `bytes.to_text_lossy`; tiktoken-rs fails there. A token that is no token fails `invalid`, its index named

capability tok/decode-bytes  tokens made bytes, all together or one by one
  heroes  tokenizer.decode_bytes, tokenizer.decode_token, tokenizer.decode_tokens
  go      -
  rust    CoreBPE::decode_bytes
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.decode_bytes, tiktoken.Encoding.decode_single_token_bytes, tiktoken.Encoding.decode_tokens_bytes, tokenizers.Tokenizer.id_to_token
  note    -

capability tok/offsets  where each token stands in the text it was made from
  heroes  tokenizer.offsets_of
  go      -
  rust    CoreBPE::split_by_token, CoreBPE::split_by_token_iter, CoreBPE::split_by_token_ordinary, CoreBPE::split_by_token_ordinary_iter
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.decode_with_offsets, tokenizers.Encoding.offsets, tokenizers.Encoding.token_to_chars, tokenizers.Encoding.char_to_token, tokenizers.OffsetReferential, tokenizers.OffsetType, tokenizers.Offsets
  note    byte indices, as a `str` is indexed; tiktoken counts characters, a token that begins inside a character given that character's index, which `unicode.floor_char_boundary` gives here. tiktoken-rs answers each token's text, `decode_token` and `bytes.to_text_lossy` here

capability tok/stream  tokens decoded one at a time as they stream, a character cut between two held
  heroes  tokenizer.decode_next
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenizers.decoders.DecodeStream
  note    -

capability tok/vocabulary  an encoding's size, its tokens and its special tokens read
  heroes  tokenizer.vocabulary_size, tokenizer.max_token, tokenizer.ranks_of, tokenizer.special_tokens, tokenizer.is_special, tokenizer.end_of_text, tokenizer.pattern_of
  go      -
  rust    CoreBPE::special_tokens
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.n_vocab, tiktoken.Encoding.max_token_value, tiktoken.Encoding.token_byte_values, tiktoken.Encoding.special_tokens_set, tiktoken.Encoding.is_special_token, tiktoken.Encoding.eot_token, tokenizers.Tokenizer.get_vocab, tokenizers.Tokenizer.get_vocab_size, tokenizers.Tokenizer.get_added_tokens_decoder
  note    tiktoken's `token_byte_values` sorts the tokens' bytes; `ranks_of` gives them by rank, which the index says

capability tok/added-tokens  tokens added to a vocabulary
  heroes  tokenizer.new, tokenizer.ranks_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tokenizers.Tokenizer.add_tokens, tokenizers.Tokenizer.add_special_tokens, tokenizers.Tokenizer.num_special_tokens_to_add
  note    an encoding is a value: one with more tokens is made by `new` from `ranks_of` and its special tokens

capability tok/batch  many texts encoded or decoded at once
  heroes  refused: a `for` over the texts does it; tiktoken's batches spread the work over threads, which are `threads`' and carry one `str` each way
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode_batch, tiktoken.Encoding.encode_ordinary_batch, tiktoken.Encoding.decode_batch, tiktoken.Encoding.decode_bytes_batch, tokenizers.Tokenizer.encode_batch, tokenizers.Tokenizer.encode_batch_fast, tokenizers.Tokenizer.decode_batch, tokenizers.Tokenizer.async_encode, tokenizers.Tokenizer.async_encode_batch, tokenizers.Tokenizer.async_encode_batch_fast, tokenizers.Tokenizer.async_decode_batch
  note    -

capability tok/unstable  the stable tokens of a prompt and every token sequence a completion could begin with
