dropped
  go      Tiktoken's and CoreBPE's fields: the parts an encoding holds, read here through its functions
  rust    CoreBPE::borrow, borrow_mut, clone, clone_from, clone_into, clone_to_uninit, from, into, to_owned, try_from, try_into, type_id: Rust's traits on every type
  rust    CoreBPE::_decode_native_and_split: the bytes of each token, `decode_tokens`
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.encode_to_numpy: an array of NumPy, which Heroes has not
  python  tiktoken.Encoding._encode_bytes, tiktoken.Encoding._encode_only_native_bpe: tiktoken's private helpers; bytes not UTF-8 are `encode_piece`'s
  python  tiktoken.core, tiktoken.load, tiktoken.model, tiktoken.registry: the modules the package is made of; tiktoken.load.annotations, base64, hashlib, os, tiktoken.model.Encoding, tiktoken.model.get_encoding, tiktoken.model.annotations, tiktoken.registry.Any, Callable, Sequence, functools, importlib, pkgutil, threading, tiktoken, tiktoken_ext, Encoding, annotations: names the modules import
  python  tiktoken.Encoding.name: the record's field `name`
  python  tokenizers.Tokenizer.model, normalizer, pre_tokenizer, post_processor, decoder: the parts a tokenizer of Hugging Face is assembled from, which an `Encoding` holds as its pattern and tables
  python  tokenizers.implementations, tokenizers.BertWordPieceTokenizer, tokenizers.ByteLevelBPETokenizer, tokenizers.CharBPETokenizer, tokenizers.SentencePieceBPETokenizer, tokenizers.SentencePieceUnigramTokenizer: ready-made assemblies of the parts above
  python  tokenizers.EncodeInput, InputSequence, PreTokenizedEncodeInput, PreTokenizedInputSequence, TextEncodeInput, TextInputSequence, Enum, List, Tuple, Union, Token: type aliases and the typing module's names
  python  tokenizers.tokenizers, tokenizers.models.models, tokenizers.pre_tokenizers.pre_tokenizers, tokenizers.decoders.decoders, tokenizers.processors.processors: the compiled module and its submodules
